# Local runtime state (database, snapshots, node config, coverage/track
# archives) must never ship in the image. Docker seeds a fresh named volume
# from whatever the image holds at that path, so a developer's own
# create_all-built users.db baked in here means every clean deploy boots
# against a database that already has the auth tables: 0001 early-returns
# and stamps itself, then 0002's plain CREATE TABLE hits "table nodes already
# exists" and the (correct) migration-failure abort refuses to boot.
# The directory itself is kept: core/users.py expects backend/data to exist,
# and backend/data/README.md is what holds it in git.
backend/data/*
!backend/data/README.md
# Same problem, no tracked placeholder needed: purely local synthetic-fleet
# and coverage-run output, recreated on demand by services/storage.py.
backend/coverage_data/
# Same problem, no tracked placeholder needed: the built image would otherwise
# carry a stale aircraft.json snapshot and a receiver.json holding the lat/lon
# of whichever machine last wrote it. Not needed at build time; the Dockerfile
# creates the directory unconditionally.
backend/tar1090_data/
